		</div><!-- #post-## -->

		
	


			<div id="post-31687" class="post-31687 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-discourse-net">
			<h2 class="entry-title"><a href="https://www.discourse.net/2022/03/mysterious-traffic-spike-in-november-2020/" title="Permalink to Mysterious Traffic Spike&#8211;in November 2020" rel="bookmark">Mysterious Traffic Spike&#8211;in November 2020</a></h2>

			<div class="entry-meta">
				<span class="meta-prep meta-prep-author">Posted on</span> <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2022/03/mysterious-traffic-spike-in-november-2020/" title="9:15 am" rel="bookmark"><span class="entry-date">March 28, 2022</span></a> <span class="meta-sep">by</span> <span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://www.discourse.net/author/michael/" title="View all posts by Michael Froomkin">Michael Froomkin</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->

				<div class="entry-content">
				<p>Normally, I don&#8217;t spend much&#8211;well, really, any&#8211;time worrying about blog traffic. <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2018/09/15-years-of-blogging/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">I used to work at encouraging traffic, but, as I have explained previously, I stopped a long time ago</a>. Once in a while a post triggers an email from an old friend or acquaintance, and that makes me happy, unless they hated in it, in which case, whatever. But <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2022/03/for-my-russian-readers/">yesterday&#8217;s post for Russian readers</a> had me <a href="http://clustrmaps.com/site/m9?utm_source=widget&amp;utm_campaign=widget_ctr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">clicking on the little map in the right column</a>, and that led me to glance at the stats.  They&#8217;re under-counts, since anyone who blocks cookies or some other things won&#8217;t be counted, and lots of my friends are in the privacy and tech community and likely block more than enough stuff not to be counted. But they do tell me something about trends.  And there sure was a big spike in the data back in September 2020:</p>
<p><a href="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1.png"><img decoding="async" data-attachment-id="31689" data-permalink="https://www.discourse.net/2022/03/mysterious-traffic-spike-in-november-2020/sept2020traffic-2/" data-orig-file="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1.png" data-orig-size="1008,408" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="Sept2020traffic" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1-400x162.png" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-31689" src="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1.png" alt="" width="504" height="204" srcset="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1.png 1008w, https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1-250x101.png 250w, https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1-400x162.png 400w, https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1-150x61.png 150w, https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2022/03/Sept2020traffic-1-768x311.png 768w" sizes="(max-width: 504px) 100vw, 504px" /></a></p>
<p>Looking at the <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2020/09/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Discourse.net archive for September 2020</a>, I can&#8217;t imagine what set it off, and I don&#8217;t have logs that go so far back; I did win an award that month, but at most you&#8217;d think that would cause a few hundred hits, not eighty thousand.</p>
<p>The 40,000 in <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2020/07/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">July 2020</a> is also a mystery. My biannual local ballot recommendations for the Judicial elections are popular, but the idea that they get more than a few hundred hits at most strains credulity.</p>
<p>On the other hand, the chart just records hits and doesn&#8217;t say what they were to, so there&#8217;s no evidence that the traffic was caused by a then-recent post.  It really could be anything I&#8217;d published up to that date. Maybe some new search engine repeated Google&#8217;s old mistake and ranked my post &#8220;<a href="https://www.discourse.net/2003/11/how_not_to_pick_up_women_online">How Not To Pick Up Women Online</a>&#8221; highly for people searching for a similar phrase without the “not”.</p>
<p>Any ideas, anyone?</p>
							</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
			<div class="entry-utility">
									<span class="cat-links">
						<span class="entry-utility-prep entry-utility-prep-cat-links">Posted in</span> <a href="https://www.discourse.net/category/discourse-net/" rel="category tag">Discourse.net</a>					</span>
					<span class="meta-sep">|</span>
												<span class="comments-link"><span>Comments Off<span class="screen-reader-text"> on Mysterious Traffic Spike&#8211;in November 2020</span></span></span>
							</div><!-- .entry-utility -->
		</div><!-- #post-## -->

		
	


			<div id="post-31024" class="post-31024 post type-post status-publish format-standard hentry category-discourse-net">
			<h2 class="entry-title"><a href="https://www.discourse.net/2021/07/troubles-under-the-hood/" title="Permalink to Troubles Under the Hood" rel="bookmark">Troubles Under the Hood</a></h2>

			<div class="entry-meta">
				<span class="meta-prep meta-prep-author">Posted on</span> <a href="https://www.discourse.net/2021/07/troubles-under-the-hood/" title="1:22 pm" rel="bookmark"><span class="entry-date">July 24, 2021</span></a> <span class="meta-sep">by</span> <span class="author vcard"><a class="url fn n" href="https://www.discourse.net/author/michael/" title="View all posts by Michael Froomkin">Michael Froomkin</a></span>			</div><!-- .entry-meta -->

				<div class="entry-content">
				<p><img loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-attachment-id="31025" data-permalink="https://www.discourse.net/2021/07/troubles-under-the-hood/car/" data-orig-file="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/car.webp" data-orig-size="750,500" data-comments-opened="1" data-image-meta="{&quot;aperture&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;credit&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;camera&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;created_timestamp&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;copyright&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;focal_length&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;iso&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;shutter_speed&quot;:&quot;0&quot;,&quot;title&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;orientation&quot;:&quot;0&quot;}" data-image-title="car" data-image-description="" data-image-caption="" data-large-file="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/car.webp" class="alignright wp-image-31025" src="https://www.discourse.net/site/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/car.webp" alt="" width="433" height="289" />Discourse.net suffered a bad crash yesterday [Friday, July 23].</p>
<p>[<strong>UPDATE: Wed July 29. I&#8217;m hoping it&#8217;s fixed now?</strong>]</p>
<p>It should all be sorted out soonish, but until then, please be patient with site weirdness.</p>
<p>Sorry about that.</p>
							</div><!-- .entry-content -->
	
			<div class="entry-utility">
									<span class="cat-links">
						<span class="entry-utility-prep entry-utility-prep-cat-links">Posted in</span> <a href="https://www.discourse.net/category/discourse-net/" rel="category tag">Discourse.net</a>					</span>
					<span class="meta-sep">|</span>
												<span class="comments-link"><span>Comments Off<span class="screen-reader-text"> on Troubles Under the Hood</span></span></span>
							</div><!-- .entry-utility -->
		</div><!-- #post-## -->

		
	

